+    // SYCL command-graph capture state.
+    //
+    // A weight reorder (reorder_qw(): async_malloc + memcpy + parallel_for + async_free) is a
+    // one-time layout install whose command group cannot be recorded into a graph: the graph
+    // ends up holding a node that depends on an event recorded outside the recording region,
+    // and finalize() rejects it ("Graph nodes cannot depend on events from outside the graph").
+    // A reorder is therefore never started while recording. opt_for_reorder[_id]() only sets
+    // graph_reorder_deferred, and the op runs on the plain layout for that pass (identical
+    // numbers, just not re-ordered); graph_compute then drops the unfinished recording and
+    // re-runs the call uncaptured once, which installs the reorder exactly as the non-graph
+    // path does. The next call captures cleanly - at most one deferral per newly seen weight.
+    bool graph_recording        = false;
+    bool graph_reorder_deferred = false;
